{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) for Google Agent Harness Competition\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is intended to be uploaded to Kaggle and run as a Kaggle kernel.  It demonstrates how to:\n",
    "- list the files that belong to the competition dataset,\n",
    "- inspect a sample XLSX file,\n",
    "- extract basic metadata from PDF files,\n",
    "- optionally read an IFC (Industry Foundation Classes) model.\n",
    "\n",
    "The notebook relies on the `uv` package manager for reproducible environments.  All heavy dependencies are installed lazily in the first cell so the kernel starts quickly."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Install required libraries in the Kaggle environment\n",
    "# This cell uses `uv` which is pre‑installed in the repo.  If `uv` is not available, fall back to pip.\n",
    "!pip install uv -q\n",
    "!uv add pandas openpyxl pymupdf ifcopenshell -U -q || true"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "# Optional imports – they may fail if the optional libraries are not installed\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    import fitz  # PyMuPDF for PDF metadata\n",
    "except ImportError:\n",
    "    fitz = None\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    import ifcopenshell  # IFC file reader\n",
    "except ImportError:\n",
    "    ifcopenshell = None"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "def list_files(root: Path) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    @definition : Return a DataFrame listing files under *root* with size information.\n",
    "    @args/params : root – Path object pointing to the directory to scan.\n",
    "    @return : DataFrame with columns ['path', 'size_bytes', 'size_mb'].\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    # Walk the directory tree and collect file info\n",
    "    data = []\n",
    "    for dirpath, _, filenames in os.walk(root):\n",
    "        for fname in filenames:\n",
    "            fpath = Path(dirpath) / fname\n",
    "            size = fpath.stat().st_size\n",
    "            data.append({\n",
    "                'path': str(fpath.relative_to(root)),\n",
    "                'size_bytes': size,\n",
    "                'size_mb': size / (1024 * 1024)\n",
    "            })\n",
    "    df = pd.DataFrame(data)\n",
    "    return df.sort_values('size_mb', ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Adjust this path if your competition data lives elsewhere\n",
    "data_root = Path('')  # repository root – Kaggle kernels start in the repo folder\n",
    "files_df = list_files(data_root)\n",
    "display(files_df.head(10))\n",
    "print(f'\nTotal files: {len(files_df)} – Total size: {files_df[\'size_mb\'].sum():.2f} MiB')"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load a sample Excel file (XLSX)\n",
    "\n",
    "Replace `sample.xlsx` with the actual file name you want to explore."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "excel_path = data_root / 'sample.xlsx'  # <-- change if needed\n",
    "if excel_path.exists():\n",
    "    df_excel = pd.read_excel(excel_path)\n",
    "    display(df_excel.head())\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f'Excel file not found at {excel_path}')"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Inspect PDF metadata\n",
    "\n",
    "The code below prints the title, author and creation date of each PDF file in the dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "if fitz is not None:\n",
    "    pdf_files = [p for p in data_root.rglob('*.pdf') if p.is_file()]\n",
    "    for pdf_path in pdf_files[:5]:  # limit to first 5 PDFs for brevity\n",
    "        doc = fitz.open(pdf_path)\n",
    "        meta = doc.metadata\n",
    "        print(f'File: {pdf_path.name}')\n",
    "        print(f"  Title   : {meta.get('title')}")\n",
    "        print(f"  Author  : {meta.get('author')}")\n",
    "        print(f"  Created : {meta.get('creationDate')}")\n",
    "        print('-' * 40)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('PyMuPDF (fitz) not installed – skipping PDF metadata extraction.')"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Optional: Load an IFC file (if present)\n",
    "\n",
    "IFC files are common in architecture / construction datasets.  The snippet will list the entities of the first IFC file it finds."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "if ifcopenshell is not None:\n",
    "    ifc_files = list(data_root.rglob('*.ifc'))\n",
    "    if ifc_files:\n",
    "        ifc = ifcopenshell.open(ifc_files[0])\n",
    "        types = set(e.is_a() for e in ifc)\n",
    "        print(f'Loaded IFC: {ifc_files[0].name}')\n",
    "        print('Entity types present:', ', '.join(sorted(types)))\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print('No IFC files found in the repository.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('ifcopenshell not installed – skipping IFC inspection.')"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Next steps\n",
    "* Explore the remaining files with `list_files` and visualise distributions.\n",
    "* Perform deeper feature engineering on the XLSX sheets.\n",
    "* Use the extracted PDF metadata for document‑level analysis.\n",
    "* If you need to work with IFC geometry, consider using `ifcopenshell` utilities or converting to a mesh format."
   ]
  }
